## Disclaimer Icon Rule — "Always review AI-generated content prior to use."

Every instance of this legal disclaimer string **must** be preceded by a blue `InfoCircleIcon`.
The canonical pattern (copy exactly):

```tsx
import { InfoCircleIcon } from '@patternfly/react-icons';

<Content component="p" className="ols-ai-hub-page-disclaimer">
  <InfoCircleIcon
    style={{
      color: 'var(--pf-t--global--icon--color--status--info--default)',
      marginInlineEnd: 'var(--pf-t--global--spacer--xs)',
      verticalAlign: 'middle',
      flexShrink: 0,
    }}
    aria-hidden
  />
  Always review AI-generated content prior to use.
</Content>
```

The reference implementation is `AIHubPageV2.tsx`. Any page-level file that adds or retains
this disclaimer without the icon is non-compliant and must be corrected.

---

## Summary

**One rule to remember:** If it's visible to the user and it lives outside a `v1/` or `v3/` directory,
it must say **"run"**, not **"plan"** — and every "Always review AI-generated content prior to use."
disclaimer must have the blue `InfoCircleIcon` prefix.
